A||||5||Raydar||Speed Bleeders!||||14||
Z||000000||Raydar||08-26-2001||09:29 AM|||| <A HREF="http://www.speedbleeder.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.speedbleeder.com</A> <P>Anybody use 'em?<BR>Bought sets for all my cars. I put a pair on my Sonoma last night. <BR>They work just like advertised... <BR>Crack 'em open 1/4 turn. Connect a clear hose. Apply the brakes until there are no bubbles. Tighten it 1/4 turn. Done! <BR>They have a one-way check valve in them. Lets the fluid out. Stops anything from being sucked back in. Takes less than 5 minutes per wheel.<BR>The only thing I don't like is that they are made of brass instead of steel. But I can live with that.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||14
Z||000001||starfighter007@msn.com||08-26-2001||11:13 AM||||They look like they should work pretty good .The price seems to be pretty reasonable @$7.00 each I think I might have to get me a set .Thanks for the info ||||reg||14
Z||000002||artherd||08-26-2001||12:21 PM||||I love 'em.  bloody great stuff.  Here's a tip: *tiny* bit of thin teflon tape on the threads, this helps them seal better at the threads when open 1/4 turn.<P>SpeedBleeders are my heros!<P>(and I like the brass, dosen't corrode as easially)<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
Z||000003||recluse||08-26-2001||12:58 PM||||Those look like they will work good, I think i will get a set.  Has anyone used one on the clutch system? How did it work there? <BR>thanks||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||08-26-2001||07:26 PM||||make sure they are capped or you won't like them so much in a year or two. stuff that gets in them can plug them solid.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Monkeyman||08-26-2001||09:36 PM||||I used 'em about a year ago on the Grape Ape.  They worked great.  I'll probably buy another set (of 4) for 4Play whenever I decide to do the brakes (doesn't need brakes yet).<P>------------------<BR>'Consciousness:  That annoying time between naps.'<P>MM||||reg||1
